      "writtenOn": "2019-09-06T09:49:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, max_spare_cap_cpu is the CPU with max spare cap in the _performance domain_, while max_spare_cap_cpu_ls is the CPU with max spare cap in the entire _root domain_. And yes, max_spare_cap_cpu_ls is useless if we\u0027ve found an idle cpu, hence this \u0027else\u0027 which optimizes this case a tiny bit. I could add \u0027\u0026\u0026 best_idle_cpu \u003c 0\u0027 to the \u0027else\u0027 condition, but not sure this is really going to be any faster.",
